 Here is a YAML Semgrep rule that matches the vulnerable behavior and avoids matching the patched behavior:

```yaml
id: "vuln-novnc-ad941fad"
title: "Potential XSS in WebUtil.createCookie function"
description: |
  This rule detects potential Cross Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities in the WebUtil.createCookie function by setting a cookie with user input directly.
severity: WARNING
languages:
  - javascript
metadata:
  category: Cryptographic Issues
pattern: |-
  :[
    (
      function [$method_name] WebUtil.createCookie = function(name,value,days) {
        var date, expires;
        if (days) {
          date = new Date();
          date.setTime(date.getTime()+(days*24*60*60*1000));
          expires = "; expires="+date.toGMTString();
        } else {
          expires = "";
        }
        document.cookie = name+"="+value+expires+"; path=/";
      }
    )
  ]
```

This rule will match any function named `WebUtil.createCookie` that takes three arguments and sets a cookie with the second argument value directly into the cookie string. It does not depend on repository-specific names or functions, making it generalizable across different repositories.

